---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import StatTile from '../components/StatTile.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
import YouTube from '../components/YouTube.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { STATS } from '../data/stats';
import { fig, photo } from '../lib/assets';
import { href, SITE, repoUrl } from '../lib/site';

const hero = fig('misc/hero_render') ?? fig('slides/page-01');
const board = photo('20261004_162523');
const carpark = photo('20261020_132132');
const sun = photo('20261020_131809');
const solar = fig('analysis/S02_shade_power') ?? fig('results/solar_S02');
const paths = [
  { title: 'I’m hiring', body: 'The short version: problem, approach, what was built, what it measured, and how the work was run.', href: href('/story/'), cta: 'Read the story' },
  { title: 'I’m the next team', body: 'Build, flash, run, and every gotcha we hit, with links into the repository.', href: href('/handover/'), cta: 'Open the handover' },
  { title: 'I’m curious', body: 'Spin the hardware in 3D, scrub the design evolution, watch it run in the sun.', href: href('/hardware/'), cta: 'Explore the hardware' },
];
---
<Base theme="auto" ogImage={hero?.src}>
  <section class="hero dark-scope">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">QUT EGH490 capstone · 2026 · control stream</p>
        <h1>A string of solar panels is only as strong as its weakest module.<br /><span class="accent">We built a converter that moves the difference.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">The Power Shuffler is a differential power processor: a bidirectional interleaved buck-boost converter between neighbouring panels that shuttles only the mismatch current, so a shaded panel stops starving the string. This site is the showcase, the knowledge base and the handover.</p>
        <div class="row" style="margin-top:1.4rem">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={href('/story/')}>Start with the story</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href('/hardware/')}>Hardware in 3D</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={SITE.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-media">
        {hero && <Image src={hero} alt="Render of the shuffler board inside its 3D-printed enclosure with the Raspberry Pi pod" width={1400} loading="eager" class="hero-img" />}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section tight>
    <div class="grid grid-4">
      {STATS.map((s) => <StatTile value={s.value} label={s.label} evidence={s.evidence} href={s.href} />)}
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="60-second introduction" title="Watch it first" lede="A short walkthrough of the problem, the board and the carpark test. Longer tool tours live under Media." narrow>
    <YouTube title="Boost Brigade: the Power Shuffler in 60 seconds" note="Intro video: recorded by the team; this slot becomes the embed once the clip is uploaded (unlisted)." />
  </Section>

  <Section alt eyebrow="The story in five beats" title="From a shaded panel to 99 watts back">
    <div class="beats">
      <article class="beat reveal">
        <span class="beat-n">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>The problem: one shaded panel limits the whole string</h3>
          <p>Panels in series must carry the same current. Shade one and its bypass diode discards that panel’s power; the string’s P–V curve grows several peaks and ordinary MPPT can lock onto the wrong one.</p>
          {fig('misc/pv_mismatch_1000_200') && <Figure src={fig('misc/pv_mismatch_1000_200')!} alt="P–V curves of a string with one module at 200 W/m² and the rest at 1000 W/m²" caption="Mismatch: the string curve with one module at 200 W/m² develops a second peak." evidence={{ label: 'MIL PV figures', href: repoUrl('4_Simulink/1_MIL_Model_In_The_Loop/PV_figures') }} />}
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="beat reveal">
        <span class="beat-n">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>The idea: move the difference, not the power</h3>
          <p>A shuffler sits between two neighbouring panels. Its coupled inductor and two half-bridges push the current difference up or down the string so module voltages stay equal and every panel works at its own maximum power point. It only processes the mismatch, so losses scale with the shade, not the string.</p>
          <Diagram name="shuffler_circuit" alt="Circuit of one interleaved buck-boost shuffler between two PV modules" caption="One shuffler: two half-bridges, a coupled inductor, decoupling capacitors between neighbouring modules." />
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="beat reveal">
        <span class="beat-n">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>The control: a MIMO plant tamed by inverting its DC gain</h3>
          <p>Shufflers share panels, so their dynamics are coupled. The N-module averaged model splits each shuffler into a shuffled mode and a circulating mode with closed-form gains, and a decoupling integral controller <em>M = G⁻¹·diag(k<sub>I</sub>)</em> cancels the couplings by construction. A 1 kHz feasibility governor protects the current rating.</p>
          <Diagram name="control_loop" alt="Block diagram of the decoupling PI controller and supervisor around the string plant" caption="Control architecture: decoupling PI on [v_d, i_c], supervisor on top, 10 kHz tick." />
          <a class="btn" href={href('/control/')}>Control deep dive</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="beat reveal">
        <span class="beat-n">04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>The build: one board, two shufflers, one C core everywhere</h3>
          <p>A six-layer Version 0 board with hall current sensors and INA239 voltage monitors, driven by an STM32G474 Nucleo, with a Raspberry Pi pod streaming telemetry to Grafana. The same C control core runs in Simulink (SIL), inside QSPICE (as a DLL) and in the firmware, with gains generated from one JSON file.</p>
          {board && <Figure src={board} alt="Assembled Version 0 shuffler board with the Nucleo-G474RE, two coupled inductors and XT60 connectors" caption="4 Oct 2026: the assembled board." />}
          <a class="btn" href={href('/hardware/')}>Explore the hardware</a>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="beat reveal">
        <span class="beat-n">05</span>
        <div>
          <h3>The field: it works in the sun</h3>
          <p>20 Oct 2026, three 80 W panels in the carpark into a 61 V constant-voltage load. With the top panel shaded to almost zero current, the shufflers kept the other two delivering: up to 99 W during the shading event and 10.6 Wh over 36 minutes. The loop closed from k = 0.1 to 0.8 without a fault.</p>
          {solar && <Figure src={solar} alt="String power during the S02 shading event with the shufflers running" caption="Run S02: string power through the shade event." evidence={{ label: 'REPORT §4', href: repoUrl('8_Results/analysis/REPORT.md') }} />}
          <a class="btn" href={href('/results/')}>See the results</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Pick your path" title="Three ways in">
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      {paths.map((p) => (
        <a class="card card-link reveal" href={p.href}>
          <h3>{p.title}</h3>
          <p class="muted">{p.body}</p>
          <span class="mono small" style="color:var(--accent-ink)">{p.cta} →</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section alt tight>
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items:center">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Honest by design</p>
        <h3>Every number links to its evidence</h3>
        <p class="muted">Stat tiles, figures and claims on this site point at the report section, CSV window or source file they come from. Where a measurement is a bound rather than a value (the 44 Hz telemetry cannot resolve a 10 ms loop), the caveat is printed next to it.</p>
        <a class="btn" href={href('/results/#caveats')}>Read the caveats</a>
      </div>
      {sun && <Image src={sun} alt="The shuffler board running in the sun at the carpark test" width={900} style="border-radius:14px;border:1px solid var(--line)" />}
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6.5rem) 0 clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .hero::before { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: -20% -10% auto; height: 70%; background: radial-gradient(60% 60% at 70% 30%, rgba(255,180,0,.18), transparent 70%); pointer-events: none; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; gap: 2.5rem; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr .95fr; align-items: center; position: relative; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.2vw, 3.4rem); }
  .accent { color: var(--accent); }
  .hero-media :global(img) { border-radius: 18px; box-shadow: 0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.45); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .beats { display: grid; gap: 2.5rem; }
  .beat { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr; gap: 1rem; align-items: start; max-width: 860px; }
  .beat-n { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent-ink); font-size: 1.1rem; padding-top: .3rem; }
  .beat h3 { margin-top: 0; }
  .beat :global(.figure) { max-width: 760px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .beat { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
